    "JurisdictionSpecifics": "New York. Murder in the Second Degree under NY Penal Law § 125.25 requires proof beyond a reasonable doubt that the defendant intentionally caused the death of another person. The death penalty is not applicable — if convicted, the defendant faces a mandatory sentence of 15 years to life. The State\u0027s case is built on circumstantial evidence and two key eyewitnesses. The defense argues that reasonable doubt permeates every piece of evidence. This case is a direct adaptation of the classic \u002212 Angry Men\u0022 scenario — a seemingly open-and-shut prosecution case that unravels under careful deliberation.",
