        {
            "FileName": "Neighbor Account - The Argument.pdf",
            "FilePath": "",
            "Summary": "Statement from Ms. Rosa Alvarez, who lives in apartment 2D at 231 Delancey (across the hall from Mr. McAllister). She states that on the night of July 8, between approximately 11:30 PM and midnight, she heard loud arguing coming from the Torres apartment above her. She distinctly heard Daniel Torres shout \u0027I\u0027m going to kill you!\u0027 followed by more shouting and what sounded like furniture being knocked over. She did NOT call the police because arguing from that apartment was \u0027nothing new.\u0027 She also states she heard the argument stop abruptly, followed by a door slamming and footsteps running down the stairs. She estimates she heard the running footsteps approximately 15-20 seconds after the shouting stopped. DEFENSE NOTE: Ms. Alvarez\u0027s timeline — footsteps 15-20 seconds after the shouting stopped and a thud — is INCONSISTENT with Mr. McAllister\u0027s timeline (he claims he was at his door in time to see the fleeing figure). If the footsteps were 15-20 seconds after the thud, McAllister — who takes 40+ seconds to reach his door — could not possibly have seen anyone.",
