            "Summary": "Court-ordered psychological evaluation of Daniel Torres, conducted by Dr. Miriam Foster, forensic psychologist. Key findings: (1) Full-scale IQ of 83 (13th percentile) with particular deficits in verbal memory and processing speed. (2) Documented learning disability diagnosed at age 9. (3) History of emotional neglect and physical abuse by the decedent (Hector Torres) — multiple Child Protective Services reports, none resulted in removal. (4) No evidence of antisocial personality disorder or violent tendencies beyond the single juvenile arrest. (5) Dr. Foster opines that Torres\u0027s inability to recall film titles from the night of the murder is \u0027entirely consistent with his cognitive profile under stress\u0027 — his verbal memory is in the bottom 10th percentile. (6) Torres demonstrates genuine grief when discussing his father\u0027s death — crying, voice breaking, avoidance of photographs. Dr. Foster notes this is \u0027inconsistent with the emotional presentation of someone who has just murdered a parent.\u0027 PROSECUTION OBJECTION: The prosecution challenged the grief assessment as speculative and outside the scope of forensic psychology.",
